# Build-context exclusions for the MCP sidecar image (deploy/hermes/Dockerfile).
#
# The Dockerfile never runs `COPY .`. It copies pyproject.toml, README.md,
# src/, config/, and scripts/run_mcp_http_server.py by name, and
# tests/test_hermes_deployment_contract.py asserts it keeps doing so. That
# explicit COPY list, not this file, is what keeps `.env` out of the image.
# This file is the second line: it keeps secrets and local state out of the
# build context that is handed to the daemon in the first place, and keeps
# that context small enough for rebuilds to stay fast.
#
# Patterns are matched from the context root and are not recursive on their
# own, so anything that can appear at any depth is written with `**/`.

# Source control and local environments
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/

# Secrets and machine-local configuration
.env
.env.*

# Runtime artifacts and test state
.coverage
.mypy_cache/
.pytest-tmp/
.pytest_cache/
.tmp/
data/
evals/
htmlcov/

# Agent, spec, and editor tooling metadata: never read at runtime
.agents/
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
.specify/
.superpowers/

# Not required by the sidecar image
deploy/
docs/
specs/
tests/
HANDOFF-*
